{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' tasks/2026-07-17-socs-60image-chatgpt-prompts.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Style B — Social Studies P3–P6 — 60-image ChatGPT-pasteable prompt set\n\nGenerated directly from the approved image-design-intent manifests (`tools/image-manifest/p{3,4,5,6}-socs-image-manifest*.json`) using the Style B prompt template locked 2026-07-12 and confirmed working after the 3-image pilot test (2026-07-17, `tasks/2026-07-17-styleB-3image-qa-result.md`).\n\n**Workflow per image:**\n1. Copy the \"Prompt\" text into ChatGPT.\n2. Copy the \"Avoid\" text as a follow-up instruction (or append it to the prompt as \"Avoid: ...\").\n3. Download the result and save it under `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/` with the **exact filename** given (do not rename).\n4. Once a band (or all 60) is done, tell Claude — QA review, overlay compositing, and guarded promotion into `app/images/` happen after.\n\n**Recommended order:** one band at a time (P3 → P4 → P5 → P6), reviewing each band's results before starting the next — same discipline used for the content-authoring phase.\n\n---\n\n\n## Band P3 (15 images)\n\n### 1. `p3-socs-01` — The Meaning and Importance of Social and Citizenship Studies\n\n**Save as:** `style-b-p3-socs-01.png` → `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/style-b-p3-socs-01.png`\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Clean watercolor editorial illustration for a premium children's curriculum, landscape 3:2. A Northern Nigerian primary-school courtyard where girls and boys work together: two pupils place litter in a bin, two care for shared books, and two calmly discuss a simple classroom matter with a teacher nearby, showing observation, cooperation, rules, and care for public property. Translucent controlled watercolor with high-contrast focal objects and no pale or muddy washes, bright paper-white negative space, selective indigo/pencil contours around important silhouettes, clear educational visual hierarchy, culturally grounded Northern Nigerian details. Keep the upper 22% band and left/right label-safe margins completely unpainted: no wash, texture, line, icon, or incidental detail. Do not include any writing, symbols, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, anatomy-relationship lines, or circuit/wire connections in the illustration; these are added only by the separate overlay compositing step.\n\n**Avoid:**\n\n> No text, letters, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, rendered anatomy-relationship lines, rendered circuit/wire connections, watermark, logo, brand, photorealism, generic flat icon set, pale or muddy wash, dark muddy wash, low-contrast focal objects, over-rendered texture, pseudo-African patterning, caricature, unsafe child behavior, plant damage, distorted anatomy, or rendered callout labels. Show equal participation by girls and boys; no religious, ethnic, political-party, or status symbols; do not portray any child as naturally obedient, disruptive, or dominant because of gender or background.\n\n**Deterministic overlay labels (NOT part of the prompt — added later by the compositor):** Haɗin kai, Kayan jama’a\n\n---\n\n### 2. `p3-socs-02` — Our Local Government Area\n\n**Save as:** `style-b-p3-socs-02.png` → `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/style-b-p3-socs-02.png`\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Clean watercolor editorial illustration for a premium children's curriculum, landscape 3:2. A simple, non-geographic community map connecting a neutral local government (LGA) office to a market, a water point, a school, a health centre, and a clean local road; small diverse groups of residents give information to an office worker and use the services. Translucent controlled watercolor with high-contrast focal objects and no pale or muddy washes, bright paper-white negative space, selective indigo/pencil contours around important silhouettes, clear educational visual hierarchy, culturally grounded Northern Nigerian details. Keep the upper 22% band and left/right label-safe margins completely unpainted: no wash, texture, line, icon, or incidental detail. Do not include any writing, symbols, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, anatomy-relationship lines, or circuit/wire connections in the illustration; these are added only by the separate overlay compositing step.\n\n**Avoid:**\n\n> No text, letters, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, rendered anatomy-relationship lines, rendered circuit/wire connections, watermark, logo, brand, photorealism, generic flat icon set, pale or muddy wash, dark muddy wash, low-contrast focal objects, over-rendered texture, pseudo-African patterning, caricature, unsafe child behavior, plant damage, distorted anatomy, or rendered callout labels. Use no real seal, party colour, candidate portrait, campaign sign, named office-holder, or claim that one authority alone provides every service; depict women and men as residents and workers.\n\n**Deterministic overlay labels (NOT part of the prompt — added later by the compositor):** Ofishin Ƙaramar Hukuma, Kasuwa, Wurin ruwa, Makaranta, Cibiyar lafiya\n\n---\n\n### 3. `p3-socs-03` — Community Needs and Services\n\n**Save as:** `style-b-p3-socs-03.png` → `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/style-b-p3-socs-03.png`\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Clean watercolor editorial illustration for a premium children's curriculum, landscape 3:2. A child-friendly community-needs map with paired need-and-service examples: clean water and a repaired pump, learning and a school, health and a health centre, safe passage and a drained road, plus pupils reporting a problem to an adult rather than repairing hazards themselves. Translucent controlled watercolor with high-contrast focal objects and no pale or muddy washes, bright paper-white negative space, selective indigo/pencil contours around important silhouettes, clear educational visual hierarchy, culturally grounded Northern Nigerian details. Keep the upper 22% band and left/right label-safe margins completely unpainted: no wash, texture, line, icon, or incidental detail. Do not include any writing, symbols, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, anatomy-relationship lines, or circuit/wire connections in the illustration; these are added only by the separate overlay compositing step.\n\n**Avoid:**\n\n> No text, letters, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, rendered anatomy-relationship lines, rendered circuit/wire connections, watermark, logo, brand, photorealism, generic flat icon set, pale or muddy wash, dark muddy wash, low-contrast focal objects, over-rendered texture, pseudo-African patterning, caricature, unsafe child behavior, plant damage, distorted anatomy, or rendered callout labels. Children must only observe and report; do not show them entering drains, handling tools, repairing pumps, directing traffic, or doing hazardous sanitation work.\n\n**Deterministic overlay labels (NOT part of the prompt — added later by the compositor):** Ruwa mai tsabta, Hidimar jama’a, Magudanar ruwa, Cibiyar lafiya\n\n---\n\n### 4. `p3-socs-04` — Transportation — Road and Rail\n\n**Save as:** `style-b-p3-socs-04.png` → `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/style-b-p3-socs-04.png`\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Clean watercolor editorial illustration for a premium children's curriculum, landscape 3:2. Two side-by-side transport scenes: a calm paved road with a car, bicycle, and produce truck, and a passenger train moving on a fenced rail line; a separate safe-crossing inset shows a child with an adult stopping and looking both ways away from the tracks. Translucent controlled watercolor with high-contrast focal objects and no pale or muddy washes, bright paper-white negative space, selective indigo/pencil contours around important silhouettes, clear educational visual hierarchy, culturally grounded Northern Nigerian details. Keep the upper 22% band and left/right label-safe margins completely unpainted: no wash, texture, line, icon, or incidental detail. Do not include any writing, symbols, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, anatomy-relationship lines, or circuit/wire connections in the illustration; these are added only by the separate overlay compositing step.\n\n**Avoid:**\n\n> No text, letters, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, rendered anatomy-relationship lines, rendered circuit/wire connections, watermark, logo, brand, photorealism, generic flat icon set, pale or muddy wash, dark muddy wash, low-contrast focal objects, over-rendered texture, pseudo-African patterning, caricature, unsafe child behavior, plant damage, distorted anatomy, or rendered callout labels. No child on the carriageway or rail line, no vehicle collision, no hanging from vehicles, and no crossing in front of a moving train; keep the rail line physically separated from the pedestrian scene.\n\n**Deterministic overlay labels (NOT part of the prompt — added later by the compositor):** Hanya, Jirgin ƙasa, Layin dogo\n\n---\n\n### 5. `p3-socs-05` — Transportation — Air and Water\n\n**Save as:** `style-b-p3-socs-05.png` → `tools/image-pipeline/output/raw/style-b-p3-socs-05.png`\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Clean watercolor editorial illustration for a premium children's curriculum, landscape 3:2. Two balanced panels: a passenger aircraft at a generic airport with luggage being loaded, and a stable passenger boat on calm water carrying people and sacks of goods within capacity; every boat passenger wears a life jacket and a child sits beside an adult. Translucent controlled watercolor with high-contrast focal objects and no pale or muddy washes, bright paper-white negative space, selective indigo/pencil contours around important silhouettes, clear educational visual hierarchy, culturally grounded Northern Nigerian details. Keep the upper 22% band and left/right label-safe margins completely unpainted: no wash, texture, line, icon, or incidental detail. Do not include any writing, symbols, numbers, equations, arrows, labels, anatomy-relationship lines, or circuit/wire connections in the illustration; these are added 